            "review_title": "Review at Kichi Kichi",
            "review_text": "AnonyAdvisor\nSingapore, Singapore189 contributions\n0\nPersonal Hotpot buffet\nJul 2018 • Friends\nSo you choose what soup base you want and select your own dishes which was displayed on the conveyor belt. Generally, I find that there is not much variety on the conveyor belt. The idea of personal hot pot is fun... But once seated, you will realise there is not much thing you want to take from the conveyor belt.... unless you top up the buffet costs and the premium beef will be brought to your table. \nHowever, as we do not eat beef, there is only slices of port that you can get from the belt... There are some cooked food at the other counter.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten July 16, 2018",
